<title>VENEZUELA: Ecuador oil pipeline running normally - official.</title>
<headline>Ecuador oil pipeline running normally - official.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The transEcuadorean oil pipeline which transports almost all of the country's crude oil production was running normally on Friday evening despite a deepening political crisis and general strike in the country, a pipeline official said.</p>
<p>&quot;We're at about 370,000 barrels per day today, it's completely normal,&quot; an operations manager at SOTE, the pipeline company, told Reuters.</p>
<p>He added that oil loadings at the Pacific port of Balao were also proceeding normally and two tankers were on buoys in the harbour.</p>
<p>Ecuador produced an average of 383,858 barrels per day of crude oil in 1996, according to government figures.</p>
<p>((-- Tom Ashby, Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
